WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.886
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:08.758
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:15.077
Unit five: Travel & Transport. In this unit, you will talk about journeys and travel plans.

4
00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:16.945
Airport.

5
00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:20.562
Airport means a place where planes take off and land.

6
00:00:20.862 --> 00:00:22.641
We arrived at the airport early.

7
00:00:23.341 --> 00:00:25.982
Your turn. Say: Airport.

8
00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:29.636
Airport.

9
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.581
Passport.

10
00:00:32.281 --> 00:00:35.546
Passport means a small book you need to travel to other countries.

11
00:00:35.846 --> 00:00:37.718
Show your passport, please.

12
00:00:38.418 --> 00:00:41.198
Your turn. Say: Passport.

13
00:00:43.898 --> 00:00:44.853
Passport.

14
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.572
Journey.

15
00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:49.655
Journey means a trip from one place to another.

16
00:00:49.955 --> 00:00:51.595
The journey took five hours.

17
00:00:52.295 --> 00:00:55.249
Your turn. Say: Journey.

18
00:00:57.949 --> 00:00:58.788
Journey.

19
00:00:59.783 --> 00:01:00.715
Luggage.

20
00:01:01.415 --> 00:01:03.496
Luggage means the bags you take on a trip.

21
00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.482
Our luggage was very heavy.

22
00:01:06.182 --> 00:01:08.462
Your turn. Say: Luggage.

23
00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:12.059
Luggage.

24
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:13.796
Ticket.

25
00:01:14.496 --> 00:01:16.681
Ticket means a paper that lets you travel.

26
00:01:16.981 --> 00:01:18.737
I bought a train ticket.

27
00:01:19.437 --> 00:01:22.008
Your turn. Say: Ticket.

28
00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:25.453
Ticket.

29
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.172
Map.

30
00:01:27.872 --> 00:01:31.149
Map means a drawing of a place that shows roads and cities.

31
00:01:31.449 --> 00:01:32.694
Let's look at the map.

32
00:01:33.394 --> 00:01:35.385
Your turn. Say: Map.

33
00:01:38.085 --> 00:01:38.853
Map.

34
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:40.572
Delay.

35
00:01:41.272 --> 00:01:43.934
Delay means when something is later than planned.

36
00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.001
There was a one-hour delay.

37
00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:49.493
Your turn. Say: Delay.

38
00:01:52.193 --> 00:01:53.089
Delay.

39
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:55.108
Departure.

40
00:01:55.808 --> 00:01:57.819
Departure means leaving a place.

41
00:01:58.119 --> 00:01:59.689
Our departure is at ten.

42
00:02:00.389 --> 00:02:02.971
Your turn. Say: Departure.

43
00:02:05.671 --> 00:02:06.568
Departure.

44
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.399
Arrival.

45
00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:11.272
Arrival means coming to a place.

46
00:02:11.572 --> 00:02:13.595
The arrival time is three o'clock.

47
00:02:14.295 --> 00:02:17.226
Your turn. Say: Arrival.

48
00:02:19.926 --> 00:02:20.858
Arrival.

49
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:22.781
Customs.

50
00:02:23.481 --> 00:02:27.002
Customs means the place at the airport where officers check your bags.

51
00:02:27.302 --> 00:02:28.756
We went through customs.

52
00:02:29.456 --> 00:02:32.387
Your turn. Say: Customs.

53
00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:36.099
Customs.

54
00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:38.073
Destination.

55
00:02:38.773 --> 00:02:41.063
Destination means the place you are going to.

56
00:02:41.363 --> 00:02:43.107
Our destination is Bangkok.

57
00:02:43.807 --> 00:02:46.819
Your turn. Say: Destination.

58
00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:50.648
Destination.

59
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.593
Backpack.

60
00:02:53.293 --> 00:02:55.838
Backpack means a bag you carry on your back.

61
00:02:56.138 --> 00:02:57.615
I packed my backpack.

62
00:02:58.315 --> 00:03:00.561
Your turn. Say: Backpack.

63
00:03:03.261 --> 00:03:04.367
Backpack.

64
00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:07.487
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.855
Sreypich, are you going to travel this holiday?

66
00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.849
Yes! We're going to fly to Singapore.

67
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.732
Have you got your passport?

68
00:03:19.017 --> 00:03:21.527
Yes, and my ticket and my backpack too.

69
00:03:22.817 --> 00:03:24.201
What are you going to do there?

70
00:03:25.517 --> 00:03:27.679
We're going to visit the zoo and the gardens.

71
00:03:28.983 --> 00:03:31.947
Grammar focus: going to (future plans).

72
00:03:32.247 --> 00:03:33.944
We are going to travel next month.

73
00:03:34.244 --> 00:03:36.697
Use 'going to' for plans you have already made.

74
00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:40.533
Now read and listen. Our Trip to Singapore.

75
00:03:40.833 --> 00:03:43.436
Last holiday, my family flew to Singapore.

76
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:47.806
At the airport, we showed our passports and tickets.

77
00:03:49.117 --> 00:03:51.952
There was a short delay, so our departure was late.

78
00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:56.051
The journey took two hours, and we had lots of luggage.

79
00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.884
Next year, we are going to travel to Japan!

80
00:04:01.183 --> 00:04:03.685
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:03.985 --> 00:04:05.810
We blank going to travel next month.

82
00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.195
A, is. B, are. C, am.

83
00:04:13.183 --> 00:04:15.403
The answer is B: are.

84
00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:18.568
The place you are going to is your blank.

85
00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:23.322
A, destination. B, departure. C, luggage.

86
00:04:27.317 --> 00:04:29.885
The answer is A: destination.

87
00:04:31.383 --> 00:04:34.114
A small book you need to travel abroad is a blank.

88
00:04:34.414 --> 00:04:37.824
A, passport. B, ticket. C, map.

89
00:04:41.817 --> 00:04:43.979
The answer is A: passport.

90
00:04:45.483 --> 00:04:49.761
Now it's your turn to speak. What is the best way to travel long distances?

91
00:04:55.061 --> 00:05:00.419
I think the best way is by plane because it is fast. Next year, I'm going to fly to Japan.

92
00:05:00.719 --> 00:05:02.567
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:07.838
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and going to (future plans).

94
00:05:08.138 --> 00:05:13.379
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

95
00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.308
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

96
00:05:16.608 --> 00:05:19.226
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

